    "plain_language": "A national shock common to every department in the same year is the largest single identified factor in year-on-year pulse area change. Last season's weather and the department's soil add nothing measurable once that and a persistent department effect are accounted for, and a model given only pre-decision information does not beat assuming no change. On this evidence the shift to pulses is NOT weather-driven. The most likely drivers - price, PAC coupled aid and contract availability - are exactly the series this repo has no usable history for, so this cannot be pushed further without new data."
